    "notes": "Inspected 62 current frames: 11 portable, 11 shared-material/geographic, 23 medium-fi and 17 native. The main crossing retains paired swept walkway canopies, inclined ribs, curved tubular carriers, concrete haunched girders and flared pier walls, rounded cornices, outside walks, dark open railings, cable-linked lamps and pale beacon caps. Small landing caps were widened for one generalized map path edge. Replaced an aliased hard-cut perforation graph with the existing filtered fractional-coverage graph; canopy form remains legible across views and modes. Far levels simplify fittings while retaining the distinctive paired canopy silhouette."
  },
