    "notes": "The named standard PMTiles main crossing Ura e Ibrit / Most na Ibru (name:en Iber Bridge), mapped outside sidewalks and ordinary-photo location match resolve the previously unknown axis. No exact-QID map footprint is claimed. Anchor [20.86601972579956,42.891292885499894], heading 1.848488636959144: +X north/northwest toward the northern bank, -X south/southeast, +Z east/northeast along the Ibar. The mapped transport extent is 98.949 m; the body uses the nominal 91.2 m reference and an inferred 23.2 m width with flared landing caps. Source datum 498.8518249511719 m follows native water 499.651825 m and a declared bank/crown grade. All 24 actual map boundary width samples have model support at every LOD. Nearest upward-facing pavement meets within 0.042936 m. Two higher native bank-edge surfaces remain 0.113463 m and 0.177719 m above the cap, with joining pavement verified beneath them; those steps are recorded separately. These are renderer checks, not surveyed geographic accuracy."
  },
